            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "ikvm_input.cpp",
                    "line": 271,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Min Wang",
                        "email": "wangmin@phytium.com.cn",
                        "username": "wangmin239"
                    },
                    "message": "Compared to the original formula x * (SHRT_MAX + 1), it does not cause overflow and yields a larger result than your patched formula x * SHRT_MAX. Additionally, overflow will not occur in practice even at 8K resolution. Therefore, I believe casting x to uint32_t is unnecessary."
                },
                {
                    "file": "ikvm_input.cpp",
                    "line": 271,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jae Hyun Yoo",
                        "email": "jae.yoo@oss.qualcomm.com",
                        "username": "jaehyoo"
                    },
                    "message": "Good point. The uint32_t cast was defensive \u2014 x * SHRT_MAX only overflows int32_t once W gets past ~65535, which isn't a realistic resolution. I'll drop the cast. Updated in patch set #2."
                },
                {
                    "file": "ikvm_input.cpp",
                    "line": 274,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Min Wang",
                        "email": "wangmin@phytium.com.cn",
                        "username": "wangmin239"
                    },
                    "message": "Could you please also fix this hard-coded part while you're at it?\nmemcpy(&input->pointerReport[1], &xx, sizeof(xx));"
                },
                {
                    "file": "ikvm_input.cpp",
                    "line": 274,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jae Hyun Yoo",
                        "email": "jae.yoo@oss.qualcomm.com",
                        "username": "jaehyoo"
                    },
                    "message": "Good catch. Let's fix those parts using this patch. I've replaced both hard-coded 2s with sizeof(xx) / sizeof(yy) in patch set #2."
                }
            ],
